{
  "id": "coaction-effect",
  "term": "coaction effect",
  "definition": "The coaction effect is a change in a person's or animal's behavior or task performance that happens when another member of the same species is present and actively doing the task at the same time. It is a form of social influence in which a co-performer's presence can improve performance.",
